From: yuma shimizu <46545607+mouseos@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] native-board-init-hook: optional board initialization hook

With XNU_BOARD_INIT=1 (CONFIG_XNU_BOARD_INIT=y) bsd_init calls unixnu_board_init(), which a device
repository supplies in an archive named by XNU_EXTRA_LD_ARCHIVES. Boards without the flag build the
unchanged bsd_init.

--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -507,6 +507,16 @@
 
 	printf(copyright);
 
+#if defined(XNU_BOARD_INIT) && XNU_BOARD_INIT
+	/*
+	 * Board hook: a device repository links an archive (XNU_EXTRA_LD_ARCHIVES) that defines unixnu_board_init().
+	 * It runs once, early in bsd_init, with IOKit, the scheduler and ml_io_map available, before the root mount.
+	 */
+	{
+		extern void unixnu_board_init(void);
+		unixnu_board_init();
+	}
+#endif
 #if CONFIG_DEV_KMEM
 	bsd_init_kprintf("calling dev_kmem_init\n");
 	dev_kmem_init();
